.TH "state_handle_get_var" "3" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server library"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

int state_handle_get_var(int wfd, const char *arg);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Handles the \f[CR]GET\-VAR\f[R] protocol command.
Looks up a shell variable by name using \f[CR]find_variable()\f[R], then
sends the variable\(cqs value (base64\-encoded) and attributes back to
the client via the v1 line\-oriented protocol.
.PP
\f[B]Response format:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
VALUE <name> <base64\-value> [<attrs>]
.EE
.PP
Where \f[CR]<attrs>\f[R] is a comma\-separated list of attribute names
(e.g., \f[CR]exported,readonly,integer\f[R]).
The attrs field is omitted if the variable has no special attributes.
.PP
If the variable is not found:
.IP
.EX
ERR variable not found: <name>
.EE
.PP
If the argument is empty:
.IP
.EX
ERR variable name required
.EE
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]wfd\f[R] \(em File descriptor for writing the response via
\f[CR]protocol_write_line()\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]arg\f[R] \(em Variable name to look up.
Must not be NULL or empty.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 in all cases (errors are reported as protocol responses, not
as return values).
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]state_operations\f[R](3), \f[CR]protocol_write_line\f[R](3),
\f[CR]protocol_base64_encode\f[R](3)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Uses the v1 line\-oriented protocol (\f[CR]protocol_write_line\f[R]),
not v2 JSON frames.
.IP \(bu 2
The variable value is taken from \f[CR]var\->value\f[R].
If the value is NULL (variable exists but has no value), an empty string
is encoded.
.IP \(bu 2
Supported attribute flags: \f[CR]exported\f[R], \f[CR]readonly\f[R],
\f[CR]integer\f[R], \f[CR]local\f[R], \f[CR]array\f[R],
\f[CR]assoc\f[R], \f[CR]nameref\f[R], \f[CR]uppercase\f[R],
\f[CR]lowercase\f[R], \f[CR]capcase\f[R], \f[CR]trace\f[R].
